111	    const requestStartedAtUtc = new Date().toISOString();
112	    const rawCapture = await app.getAXStateAndScreenshot({emit:false,disableDiffing:true});
113	    const requestEndedAtMonotonic = clock();
114	    const requestEndedAtUtc = new Date().toISOString();
115	    requireFact(Number.isFinite(requestStartedAtMonotonic) && Number.isFinite(requestEndedAtMonotonic)
116	      && requestEndedAtMonotonic >= requestStartedAtMonotonic && typeof rawCapture?.state === 'string',
117	    'CAPTURE_INCOMPLETE');
```
```js
121	    const monotonicInterval = Object.freeze({start_ms:requestStartedAtMonotonic,end_ms:requestEndedAtMonotonic,
122	      duration_ms:requestEndedAtMonotonic-requestStartedAtMonotonic});
...
129	    // The capture interval starts before CUA and never renews during persistence/OCR.
130	    latest = Object.freeze({frameId,at:requestStartedAtMonotonic,capturedAt:requestStartedAtUtc,
131	      requestStartedAtUtc,requestEndedAtUtc,monotonicInterval,observation,saved,capture});
```
Validation: both monotonic endpoints must be finite numbers and `end >= start`, else `CAPTURE_INCOMPLETE` (L115–117). The UTC pair is `new Date().toISOString()` sampled immediately around the same capture call (L111, L114). `capturedAt` passed to retain/classify and stored in `latest` is the **start** UTC time (L123, L126, L130). `monotonicInterval.duration_ms` is computed as `end - start` (L122).

**Navigation `observe` (L504–520):** same pattern with `started`/`ended` (L504, L506), same finiteness/order validation (`CAPTURE_INCOMPLETE`, L507–508), same frozen `monotonicInterval {start_ms,end_ms,duration_ms}` (L512), same `capturedAt = requestStartedAtUtc` in retain/classify (L513, L516), stored as `latest.started` (L519).

**5-second freshness rule (L90–92 and L522–525):**
```js
90	  function fresh(frameId) {
91	    requireFact(!stopped && latest && latest.frameId === frameId && clock() >= latest.at && clock()-latest.at <= 5000,'FRESH_CAPTURE_REQUIRED');
92	  }
```
```js
522	  function fresh(frameId) {
523	    requireFact(latest&&latest.frameId===frameId&&clock()>=latest.started&&clock()-latest.started<=5000,
524	      'FRESH_CAPTURE_REQUIRED');
525	  }
```
The compared timestamps are the **current `clock()`** (monotonic; `performance.now()` by default) versus `latest.at` / `latest.started`, which is the **capture-request-start** monotonic value (L110 → L130; L504 → L519) — not the retain or classify completion time. The window is `<= 5000` ms and also requires `clock() >= latest.at`.

Freshness is checked at: transaction L148 (`openAlbum`), L158 (`calibrateMenu`), L214 and L219 (`originalIntent`, before and after the bridge call), L240 (`originalAtomicDispatch`), L299/L312/L314/L317 (`exactChooser`), L377/L383/L391 (`exactChooserV2`), L468 (`boundedScroll`); navigation L527 (`returnToAlbums`), L538 (`boundedScroll`).

Related non-freshness time gates in the dispatch path: permit `deadline:latest.at+5000` (L227); `clock()-permit.issuedAt<=2000` else `PERMIT_EXPIRED` (L243); `clock()>=permit.issuedAt && clock()<=permit.deadline` else `PERMIT_EXPIRED_BEFORE_MENU_CAPTURE` (L252) and `PERMIT_EXPIRED_BEFORE_SAVE_ALL` (L267).

